/Title (Over-occupied homes can create health and safety concerns while placing additional pressure on neighborhood parking, utilities, and other public services. Many of the parking concerns reported throughout Vineyard are connected to homes with more occupants and vehicles than the property was designed to accommodate. Addressing over-occupancy is an important part of improving parking availability, maintaining access for emergency vehicles, and preserving the safety and livability of our neighborhoods.)
